# Chunked emission for the bootstrap (DESIGN.md 7a stage 6), written in A0. `emitchunkio` is
# the entry of a0c-stage1/2/3 (tools/bootstrap.ts): it compiles one chunk of a program with the
# A0 front end (131072 source bytes, parse.a0 `fecap`) and the C emitter (emit_c.a0 `cunit` and `emitc`), so a program over the
# source limit is compiled a chunk at a time. `emitachunkio` is the same with the arm64 emitter
# (emit_arm64.a0 `qunit`), the entry of the arm64 stages (tools/bootstrap-arm64.ts); its output
# is assembly text where `emitchunkio` writes C, and its prelude (head 1) the two copy helpers.
# A chunk of a program in several chunks is: a header prelude (a function whose header names
# every header type of the whole program, in a fixed order, so that every chunk interns the
# same type table and the typedef names `a0t<index>` agree across chunks), the header of every
# function the chunk calls with a stub body, then the chunk's functions. Functions [from, nfns)
# are checked (given the iteration bounds of the earlier functions, read from the input) and
# emitted; the prelude and the stubs are only parsed. The C prelude and the typedefs of every
# type are written when head is 1.
# Input words: n, n source bytes, head, strict, from, then `from` iteration bounds. strict is 1
# for a program in several chunks: a body that builds a type no header names is then code 5,
# since its typedef index would differ between chunks. A program in one chunk (head 1, from 0)
# is compiled as `emitcio` compiles it.
# Output words when the code is 0: the C bytes, one per word, then the k = nfns - from
# iteration bounds of the chunk's functions (passed back with later chunks' stubs), then k.
# Nothing is written otherwise. The result is the diagnostic code (1 parse, 2 structure,
# 3 type, 4 limit, 5 above).

# `emitwasmio` is the entry of the A0 wasm32 emitter (compiler/emit_wasm.a0) and of the A0
# optimizer (compiler/optimize.a0), driven by tools/selfhost-wasm.ts: its first input word is the
# mode, 1 a source chunk (the input of `emitchunkio`, then the variant count before the chunk and
# the call table (index, depth) of the chunk's first `from` functions), 2 a chunk as checked
# tables, 3 the module linker, 8 the table entry of the optimizer (`ozopt1`, for compiler/shape.a0;
# the same function as 7), 7 the optimizer on ONE function (`ozone`; one run a function so
# that no value of the run holds more than a function and its callees: a single A0 value, a
# fold state included, is at most 65536 words). The wasm modes run on optimized tables: the
# driver optimizes the functions of a program in program order, feeding each run the optimized
# bodies of the callees it asks for. The result is the diagnostic code (6 for an unknown mode;
# for mode 7: 7 when the optimizer needs the bodies of the functions it wrote after its input,
# followed by their count; 4 when a limit of the optimizer was reached).

use "emit_arm64.a0"
use "optimize.a0"
use "shape.a0"

# `read` as a function: its (u32,io) result is named by this header, so the prelude interns it
fn rdword io -> (u32,io)
r read p0
ret r
end
# iteration bound p1 of the input into the paged table
fn rdfst (u32x128x8,io) u32 -> (u32x128x8,io)
fs at p0 0
tk at p0 1
r call rdword tk
v at r 0
t at r 1
pi shr p1 7
wi and p1 127
pg get fs pi
pg2 set pg wi v
fs2 set fs pi pg2
o rec fs2 t
ret o
end
# iteration bound p3 + p1 of the paged table
fn wfst io u32 u32x128x8 u32 -> io
i add p3 p1
pi shr i 7
wi and i 127
pg get p2 pi
v get pg wi
w write p0 v
ret w
end
# after the C: the k = p4 - p3 iteration bounds (table p2) of the chunk's functions, then k
fn wtrail io u32 u32x128x8 u32 u32 -> io
k sub p4 p3
w0 fold wfst k p0 p2 p3
w1 write w0 k
ret w1
end
# the input: (source bytes, n, iteration bounds, from, strict, head, io)
fn rdchunk io -> (u32x512x64,u32,u32x128x8,u32,bool,bool,io)
rs call readsrc p0
src at rs 0
n at rs 1
t1 at rs 2
rh call rdword t1
head at rh 0
t2 at rh 1
rt call rdword t2
strict at rt 0
t3 at rt 1
rf call rdword t3
from at rf 0
t4 at rf 1
z8 call z8
fs0 rec z8 t4
fsr fold rdfst from fs0
fst at fsr 0
t5 at fsr 1
sb ne strict 0
hd ne head 0
r rec src n fst from sb hd t5
ret r
end
fn emitchunkio io -> u32
c call rdchunk p0
src at c 0
n at c 1
fst at c 2
from at c 3
sb at c 4
hd at c 5
t5 at c 6
u call cunit t5 src n fst from sb hd
t6 at u 0
code at u 1
fstat at u 2
nfns at u 3
ok eq code 0
go select ok 1 0
t7 fold wtrail go t6 fstat from nfns
ret code
end
fn emitachunkio io -> u32
c call rdchunk p0
src at c 0
n at c 1
fst at c 2
from at c 3
sb at c 4
hd at c 5
t5 at c 6
u call qunit t5 src n fst from sb hd
t6 at u 0
code at u 1
fstat at u 2
nfns at u 3
ok eq code 0
go select ok 1 0
t7 fold wtrail go t6 fstat from nfns
ret code
end
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# wasm32 chunks: shape analyses, loop fusion and emission (compiler/shape.a0, emit_wasm.a0).
# The emitter does not `use` compiler/shape.a0 (shape.a0 uses the optimizer, which uses the
# emitter's table readers), so the orchestration lives here: `wxorch` takes the checked tables of
# a chunk (optimized by the driver, see tools/selfhost-wasm.ts) and runs, in order,
#   1. shinit, shcounts, then shpass for every function with a body (own, or an external whose
#      body the driver supplied): FILL OWN ARM OVER BORR of the shape table `sh`; a body an
#      analysis needs and does not have is listed in sh's MISS column;
#   2. when MISS is not empty the chunk is not emitted: result code 7, the chunk-function indices
#      wanted and their count (the driver adds those bodies and runs the chunk again);
#   3. else per own function (`wxfunf`, the fold body that replaces `wxfun`): shfcheck (is there a
#      fusion site: src/optimize.ts fuseLoops with recordState); if so shfuse, shfargs, shfsh give
#      the fused view of the tables, the function is emitted from it (`wxfus`), unless that code
#      calls a synthetic fused body out of line (`wxbad`: src/optimize.ts emitFused), then from the
#      unfused tables; the emitter's own requests for bodies are collected the same way;
#   4. `wachunkend`: the trailer (see `wachunk`).
# Tables: ty u32x384x65, tl u32x128x65, fns u32x128x45, nodes u32x128x132, args u32x128x512, nt
# u32x128x24 (compiler/emit_wasm.a0 `wachunk`).

# word p1 of the shape table p0
fn wshw u32x128x200 u32 -> u32
a shr p1 7
b get p0 a
c and p1 127
d get b c
ret d
end
# the shape table of the chunk p2 types: shape pass of function p8 (one trip when it has a body:
# word 6 of its row of fns, the packed ret, is 0 for a function without a body)
fn wshp1 u32x128x200 u32 u32x384x65 u32x128x65 u32x128x45 u32x128x132 u32x128x512 u32x128x24 u32 -> u32x128x200
r call shpass p0 p2 p3 p4 p5 p6 p7 p8
ret r
end
fn wshp u32x128x200 u32 u32x384x65 u32x128x65 u32x128x45 u32x128x132 u32x128x512 u32x128x24 -> u32x128x200
a mul p1 7
b add a 6
c shr b 7
d get p4 c
e and b 127
f get d e
g ne f 0
h select g 1 0
i fold wshp1 h p0 p2 p3 p4 p5 p6 p7 p1
ret i
end
# the chunk-function index p2 appended to the state's list of wanted bodies (count, list of 1024)
fn wsmq (io,u32,u32x128x16,u32,u32x128x8,u32) u32 u32 -> (io,u32,u32x128x16,u32,u32x128x8,u32)
a at p0 0
b at p0 1
c at p0 2
d at p0 3
e at p0 4
f at p0 5
g shr d 7
h and d 127
i get e g
j set i h p2
k set e g j
l add d 1
m rec a b c l k f
ret m
end
# the state with its error word set to 1 (a table of the chunk is full)
fn wserr (io,u32,u32x128x16,u32,u32x128x8,u32) u32 -> (io,u32,u32x128x16,u32,u32x128x8,u32)
a at p0 0
b at p0 1
c at p0 2
d at p0 3
e at p0 4
m rec a b c d e 1
ret m
end
# entry p1 of the shape table's list of missing bodies (MISS column, 16129..) appended to the
# list (count, table of 1024) of the first state
fn wmq (u32,u32x128x8) u32 u32x128x200 -> (u32,u32x128x8)
a at p0 0
b at p0 1
c add p1 16129
d shr c 7
e get p2 d
f and c 127
g get e f
h shr a 7
i and a 127
j get b h
k set j i g
l set b h k
m add a 1
n rec m l
ret n
end
# the call table with the entry of function p2 + p1 marked as a synthetic function: its code
# index is 2^24 (p3), which an emitted call would carry (`wxbad`)
fn wsent u32x128x16 u32 u32 u32 -> u32x128x16
a add p2 p1
b mul a 2
c call wxdts p0 0 b p3
ret c
end
# word p1 of the shape table p2 written (a fold body: the debug dump of the shape table)
fn wshd io u32 u32x128x200 -> io
a call wshw p2 p1
b write p0 a
ret b
end
# one trip: 1 when instruction p1 of the machine table p2 is a call (kind 6) to a code index of
# p3 or more
fn wbad1 u32 u32 u32x128x512 u32 -> u32
a mul p1 2
b add a 20480
c shr b 7
d get p2 c
e and b 127
f get d e
g add b 1
h shr g 7
i get p2 h
j and g 127
k get i j
l eq f 6
m ge k p3
n and l m
o select n 1 0
q or p0 o
ret q
end
# Does the code of function p0 (value variant, and the owned variant when it has one), emitted
# from these tables (p1 simd, p2 unroll, p3 fns, p4 nodes, p5 args, p6 nt, p7 ty, p8 tl, p9 type
# info, p10 shape, p11 call table with the synthetic functions marked), call a synthetic fused
# function out of line? (src/optimize.ts emitFused: then the unfused function is emitted)
fn wxbad u32 u32 u32 u32x128x45 u32x128x132 u32x128x512 u32x128x24 u32x384x65 u32x128x65 u32x128x65 u32x128x200 u32x128x16 -> bool
j call z512
k fold wxemit 1 j p0 0 0 p1 p2 p3 p4 p5 p6 p7 p8 p9 p10 p11
n call wxg k 0
b1 fold wbad1 n 0 k 16777216
h call waown p3 p8 p7 p0
i select h 1 0
l call wxg k 5
au call z512
av fold wxemit i au p0 1 l p1 p2 p3 p4 p5 p6 p7 p8 p9 p10 p11
n2 call wxg av 0
n3 select h n2 0
b2 fold wbad1 n3 0 av 16777216
b3 or b1 b2
r ne b3 0
ret r
end
# function p2 of the chunk emitted from its fused form (see the orchestration above): p0 the
# emission state, p3 simd, p4 unroll, p5 fns, p6 nodes, p7 args, p8 nt, p9 ty, p10 tl, p11 type
# info, p12 shape, p13 names, p14 fnm (the trip p1 is 0: the function is p2)
fn wxfus (io,u32,u32x128x16,u32,u32x128x8,u32) u32 u32 u32 u32 u32x128x45 u32x128x132 u32x128x512 u32x128x24 u32x384x65 u32x128x65 u32x128x65 u32x128x200 u32x128x400 u32x128x16 -> (io,u32,u32x128x16,u32,u32x128x8,u32)
fu call shfuse p9 p10 p5 p6 p7 p8 p12 p2 true
st at fu 0
ms at fu 1
nf1 at fu 2
ty2 at fu 3
tl2 at fu 4
fns2 at fu 5
nodes2 at fu 6
nt2 at fu 7
nty2 at fu 8
ar2 call shfargs p9 p10 p5 p6 p7 p8 p12 p2 true
nf0 call wshw p12 25474
sh2 call shfsh p12 ty2 tl2 fns2 nodes2 ar2 nt2 p2 nf0 nf1
a2 call wainfo ty2 tl2 nty2
ct at p0 2
nsyn sub nf1 nf0
ct2 fold wsent nsyn ct nf0 16777216
bad call wxbad p2 p3 p4 fns2 nodes2 ar2 nt2 ty2 tl2 a2 sh2 ct2
st1 eq st 1
nb select bad false true
ok and st1 nb
okc select ok 1 0
nok select ok 0 1
st7 eq st 7
c7 select st7 1 0
s0 fold wsmq c7 p0 ms
st4 eq st 4
c4 select st4 1 0
s1 fold wserr c4 s0
s2 fold wxfun okc s1 p2 p3 p4 fns2 nodes2 ar2 nt2 ty2 tl2 a2 sh2 p13 p14
s3 fold wxfun nok s2 p2 p3 p4 p5 p6 p7 p8 p9 p10 p11 p12 p13 p14
ret s3
end
# function p0 + p1 of the chunk (first function p2): `wxfun`, or `wxfus` when shfcheck finds a
# fusion site (same parameters as `wxfun`)
fn wxfunf (io,u32,u32x128x16,u32,u32x128x8,u32) u32 u32 u32 u32 u32x128x45 u32x128x132 u32x128x512 u32x128x24 u32x384x65 u32x128x65 u32x128x65 u32x128x200 u32x128x400 u32x128x16 -> (io,u32,u32x128x16,u32,u32x128x8,u32)
g add p2 p1
fc call shfcheck p9 p10 p5 p6 p7 p8 p12 g true
fd at fc 0
ms at fc 1
nm ne ms 4294967295
nmc select nm 1 0
s0 fold wsmq nmc p0 ms
has ne fd 0
hc select has 1 0
nh select has 0 1
s1 fold wxfus hc s0 g p3 p4 p5 p6 p7 p8 p9 p10 p11 p12 p13 p14
s2 fold wxfun nh s1 g p3 p4 p5 p6 p7 p8 p9 p10 p11 p12 p13 p14
ret s2
end
# A chunk of functions [p13, p14) of the checked tables (p1 ty, p2 tl, p3 fns, p4 nodes, p5 args,
# p6 nt, p7 names, p8 fnm, p9 call table of the functions before p13, p10 their iteration bounds, p11
# type count, p12 tlist words, p15 variant count before the chunk, p16 node count, p17 operand pair
# count, p18 simd, p19 unroll options): the output of `wachunk`, or code 7 with the bodies wanted
fn wxorch io u32x384x65 u32x128x65 u32x128x45 u32x128x132 u32x128x512 u32x128x24 u32x128x400 u32x128x16 u32x128x16 u32x128x8 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> (io,u32)
a call shinit p1 p2 p11
b call shcounts a p16 p17 p14 p11 p12
c fold wshp p14 b p1 p2 p3 p4 p5 p6
nown sub p14 p13
miss call wshw c 16128
dmp eq p18 5
dmpn select dmp 25600 0
io1 fold wshd dmpn p0 c
z call z8
m0 rec 0 z
m1 fold wmq miss m0 c
mc at m1 0
ml at m1 1
none eq miss 0
nodmp eq dmp false
runq and none nodmp
cnt select runq nown 0
ai call wainfo p1 p2 p11
st0 rec io1 p15 p9 mc ml 0
st fold wxfunf cnt st0 p13 p18 p19 p3 p4 p5 p6 p1 p2 ai c p7 p8
r call wachunkend st nown p10 p13 p15
ret r
end
# wasm32, mode 2: a chunk as tables, each preceded by its count: base (variants before the
# chunk), from (functions before the chunk's own: its callees outside it), the call table
# (index, depth) of those, types (triples), tlist, fns (7 words each), nodes (6 words each), the
# node types, operands (pairs), name bytes, fnm (2 words per function), then the simd option
# (0 or 1 on, 2 off, 3 and 4 dump the instruction list / the machine state of the first function
# instead of its code: tests only) and the unroll option (0: 1)
fn wam2 (io,u32) u32 -> (io,u32)
t at p0 0
rb call wardw t
base at rb 0
t1 at rb 1
rf call wardw t1
nbef at rf 0
t2 at rf 1
nd mul nbef 2
rd call warn16 t2 nd
dt at rd 0
t3 at rd 1
rn call wardw t3
nty at rn 0
t4 at rn 1
n3 mul nty 3
rt call warnty t4 n3
ty at rt 0
t5 at rt 1
rl call wardw t5
ntl at rl 0
t6 at rl 1
rtl call warn65 t6 ntl
tl at rtl 0
t7 at rtl 1
rm call wardw t7
nfn at rm 0
t8 at rm 1
n7 mul nfn 7
rfn call warn45 t8 n7
fns at rfn 0
t9 at rfn 1
rk call wardw t9
nnode at rk 0
t10 at rk 1
n6 mul nnode 6
rnd call warn132 t10 n6
nodes at rnd 0
t11 at rnd 1
rnt call warn24 t11 nnode
nt at rnt 0
t12 at rnt 1
ro call wardw t12
narg at ro 0
t13 at ro 1
n2 mul narg 2
rar call warn512 t13 n2
args at rar 0
t14 at rar 1
rnm call wardw t14
nname at rnm 0
t15 at rnm 1
rnb call warn400 t15 nname
names at rnb 0
t16 at rnb 1
nfm mul nfn 2
rfm call warn16 t16 nfm
fnm at rfm 0
t17 at rfm 1
fst call z8
rsd call wardw t17
sopt at rsd 0
t18 at rsd 1
ru call wardw t18
uopt at ru 0
t19 at ru 1
sj eq sopt 2
sk eq sopt 3
sl eq sopt 4
sd eq sopt 5
sm select sk 3 1
sn select sl 4 sm
so select sd 5 sn
simd select sj 0 so
uz eq uopt 0
unroll select uz 1 uopt
r call wxorch t19 ty tl fns nodes args nt names fnm dt fst nty ntl nbef nfn base nnode narg simd unroll
ret r
end
# the end (first free word) of the tlist words in use, as the larger of the state and the first
# parameter word + parameter count of function p1 of the table p2
fn wcnf u32 u32 u32x128x45 -> u32
a mul p1 7
b add a 1
c shr b 7
d get p2 c
e and b 127
f get d e
g add a 2
h shr g 7
i get p2 h
j and g 127
k get i j
l add f k
m gt l p0
n select m l p0
ret n
end
# the same for the record type p1 of the table p2: its fields are tlist[a .. a + b)
fn wcnt u32 u32 u32x384x65 -> u32
a call wat p2 p1 0
b call wat p2 p1 1
c call wat p2 p1 2
d eq a 5
e add b c
f select d e 0
g gt f p0
h select g f p0
ret h
end
# the node count of a chunk with p1 functions: the end of the last function's nodes
fn wcnn u32x128x45 u32 -> u32
z eq p1 0
r sub p1 1
r2 select z 0 r
a mul r2 7
b add a 4
c shr b 7
d get p0 c
e and b 127
f get d e
g add a 5
h shr g 7
i get p0 h
j and g 127
k get i j
l add f k
m select z 0 l
ret m
end
# word p1 of row p2 of the function table p0 := 0, but word 5 := p3 (a fold body over the 7 words
# of a row: the row of an opaque function holds only its node count)
fn wsw1 u32x128x45 u32 u32 u32 -> u32x128x45
a mul p2 7
b add a p1
c shr b 7
d and b 127
e eq p1 5
f select e p3 0
g get p0 c
h set g d f
i set p0 c h
ret i
end
# function p1, before the checked ones, becomes an opaque row: zeros but its node count (word
# p1 of the table p2), as the driver encodes the externals of a chunk given as tables
fn wsstub u32x128x45 u32 u32x128x16 -> u32x128x45
a shr p1 7
b get p2 a
c and p1 127
d get b c
e fold wsw1 7 p0 p1 d
ret e
end
# page p1 of the nodes table p2 (128 pages) into the 132-page table
fn wxcvn u32x128x132 u32 u32x128x128 -> u32x128x132
a get p2 p1
b set p0 p1 a
ret b
end
# wasm32 emission of the tables of a source chunk (the output of the A0 front end, nodes in
# 128-page tables): the orchestration of `wxorch` with the default options; the result is
# (io, code): 0, or 4 (a table is full), 5, 7 (bodies wanted)
fn wsorch (io,u32) u32 u32x384x65 u32x128x65 u32x128x45 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x24 u32x128x400 u32x128x16 u32x128x16 u32x128x8 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> (io,u32)
io at p0 0
z call z132
n132 fold wxcvn 128 z p5
nn call wcnn p4 p14
ntl0 fold wcnf p14 0 p4
ntl1 fold wcnt p12 ntl0 p2
r call wxorch io p2 p3 p4 n132 p6 p7 p8 p9 p10 p11 p12 ntl1 p13 p14 p15 nn p16 1 1
ret r
end
# mode 1 of the wasm tool: a source chunk through the A0 front end, then `wsorch`. Functions
# [cfrom, nfns) are checked (from the first checked function p7: the functions before it are
# stubs, whose rows become opaque rows with the node counts p8), functions [from, nfns) are
# emitted; the ones between are callee bodies the emitter asked for.
fn wsunit io u32x512x64 u32 u32x128x8 u32 u32x128x16 u32 u32 u32x128x16 -> (io,u32)
a call lexsrc p1 p2
b at a 0
c at a 1
d div c 3
e call pass1 p1 b d
f at e 1
g at e 2
h at e 3
i at e 5
j at e 7
k at e 10
l at e 11
m at e 12
n at e 15
o ne k 0
p eq l 0
q and p o
r select q 1 l
s select q d m
t call pass2 p1 f j
u at t 0
v call pass3 p1 b g i n r s d
w at v 0
x at v 2
y at v 4
z at v 5
aa at v 6
ab at v 11
ac at v 12
ad at v 18
ae at v 19
af call pass4 y ae ad
ag at af 0
ah at af 1
ai at af 2
aj at af 3
ak ne ai 0
al select ak ai ab
am select ak aj ac
an call pass5 ag ah p1 b g h d al am 0
ao at an 0
ap at an 1
aq at an 2
ar at an 5
as call bodyargs aq ar ag ah p1 b g h d al am
au at e 7
av at e 8
aw at t 1
ax at v 19
ay at v 5
az at v 6
a0 at an 4
a1 call fecap b d au aw av ax ay az a0 ar
a2 at an 8
a3 select a1 4 a2
# after a parse error the function count may be below p4: nothing is checked then
a4 call cumin p7 ad
a5 call checkir w x ao ap as p3 z aa ad a4
a6 at a5 0
a7 at a5 2
a8 at a5 4
a9 at a5 7
ba at a5 8
bb at a5 10
bc add j 127
bd shr bc 7
be call z64
bf rec be 0
bg fold cstpg bd bf f
bh at bg 0
bi call z16
bj fold cfnm ad bi ao f bh
bk eq a3 0
bl select bk bb a3
bm eq bl 0
bn select bm 1 0
afix fold wsstub p7 ao p8
st0 rec p0 0
bo fold wsorch bn st0 a6 a7 afix ap as a8 u bj p5 a9 ba p4 ad p6 ar
bio at bo 0
bec at bo 1
bok eq bl 0
bcd select bok bec bl
bp rec bio bcd
ret bp
end
# wasm32, mode 1: a source chunk (the input of `emitchunkio`), then the variant count before the
# chunk, the call table (index, depth) of the chunk's first `from` functions, the first checked
# function cfrom (<= from) and the node counts of the functions before it
fn wam1 (io,u32) u32 -> (io,u32)
t at p0 0
c call rdchunk t
src at c 0
n at c 1
fst at c 2
from at c 3
t5 at c 6
rb call rdword t5
base at rb 0
t6 at rb 1
nd mul from 2
rd call warn16 t6 nd
dt at rd 0
t7 at rd 1
rc call rdword t7
cfrom at rc 0
t8 at rc 1
rn call warn16 t8 cfrom
cnt at rn 0
t9 at rn 1
u call wsunit t9 src n fst from dt base cfrom cnt
ret u
end
fn wam3 (io,u32) u32 -> (io,u32)
t at p0 0
r call walink t
ret r
end
# mode 7: the optimizer on one function (compiler/optimize.a0 `ozone`)
fn wam7 (io,u32) u32 -> (io,u32)
t at p0 0
r call ozone t
ret r
end
# mode 8: the image of `ozopt1` (the table entry of the optimizer), same input as mode 7 without
# the summaries and the stage
fn wam8 (io,u32) u32 -> (io,u32)
t at p0 0
r call ozimg t
ret r
end
fn emitwasmio io -> u32
r call rdword p0
m at r 0
t at r 1
s0 rec t 6
m1 eq m 1
m2 eq m 2
m3 eq m 3
m7 eq m 7
m8 eq m 8
c1 select m1 1 0
c2 select m2 1 0
c3 select m3 1 0
c7 select m7 1 0
c8 select m8 1 0
a fold wam1 c1 s0
b fold wam2 c2 a
c fold wam3 c3 b
d fold wam7 c7 c
e fold wam8 c8 d
code at e 1
ret code
end
